From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:55:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] inputmethod: a keyboard that is not the input method
 hears a second touch and keeps the field in view

Row 71 of the edition: in Japanese, Korean and Chinese sessions Fcitx 5 is
KWin's input method and Plasma Keyboard is Fcitx 5's on-screen keyboard, a
second program with a layer-shell window.

- A text field's request for the keyboard (text-input v2 and v3
  show_input_panel, the internal context's request), also from a field that
  already has the focus, is now said: InputMethod::showRequested(), relayed
  as the scriptable D-Bus signal showRequested() of org.kde.kwin.VirtualKeyboard.
  activeChanged alone says nothing of a second touch on a focused field,
  so such a keyboard did not show for it.
- org.kde.kwin.VirtualKeyboard.setOnScreenKeyboardShown(bool): the calling
  process's shown layer-shell window is its keyboard. While it is shown and
  KWin's own panel is not shown at the bottom, updateInputPanelState() gives
  that window's frame to the focused window's setVirtualKeyboardGeometry()
  and to text-input v2's input_panel_state, as for KWin's own panel: the
  window ends where the keyboard begins (full-screen and desktop windows,
  and the "overlay" option, as before) and gets its place back when the
  keyboard says it is hidden, its window closes or the caller leaves the
  bus. No coordinates are taken from the caller.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
